//! `pyclipper.PyclipperOffset` (Clipper 6.4.2) for a single closed polygon with round joins, as used
//! by PaddleX's DB `unclip`.
//!
//! pyclipper works on integer coordinates: the float box corners are truncated toward zero when
//! they are added, offset points are rounded half away from zero, and round joins use
//! `ArcTolerance = 0.25` (Clipper2's floating-point offset with its default arc tolerance yields
//! different vertices). The union that Clipper runs afterwards only removes duplicate and
//! collinear vertices for the convex inputs DB produces.
//!
//! Ported from Clipper 6.4.2 (`ClipperOffset::AddPath`, `FixOrientations`, `DoOffset`,
//! `OffsetPoint`, `DoRound`), Copyright Angus Johnson 2010-2017:
